    // Climate 1, the Southeast and Centre-West: an air-conditioning summer
    // afternoon peak and a winter evening peak (lighting and electric
    // showers). Climate 2, the South: hot summer afternoons and the
    // strongest winter evening peak, with a winter monthly bump. Climate 3,
    // the tropical North and Northeast: little seasonal change, with an
    // afternoon and an evening peak all year. The hourly shapes, the
    // month-to-shape assignment and the monthly factors are authoring
    // judgments on the system clock (no sourced hourly load profile was
    // found). The summer afternoon peak follows the SIN's instantaneous
    // demand records of 102,810 MW on 22 January 2025 and 103,335 MW at 14:37
    // on 11 February 2025, driven by heat and air conditioning (Cenario
    // Energia, 2025-02-12, "ONS supera recorde de demanda instantanea de
    // carga no SIN").
